                <pb facs="0826" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews files, lot 53 D 413: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United Nations Command (Clark)
                        to the Joint Chiefs of Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-02-23T16:49:00+09:00">February 23, 1953—4:49
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>C 61314. Subj is Interim Report Current Status ROK Financial Negot.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>On 21 Feb Pres Rhee accepted proposed UNC note drafted along lines
                        previous msgs. Agmt apparently reached settlement $82,800,000 for United
                        States oblig prior to 16 Dec 52. This figure rep compromise to our initial
                        offer of $79,739,187.88. Rhee directed Paik verbally in presence my rep to
                        accept UNC proposal. Conversations with Paik on 22 Feb proceeded satis.
                        Believe solution can be reached on escalator clause. No apparent objection
                        use of Pusan wholesale price index to determine initial mil conversion rate
                        and for subsequent periodic adjustments; initial rate calculation will be
                        keyed to Pusan wholesale price index-mil conversion rate relationship of Apr
                        51. Ques of drawings heretofore made subsequent to 16 Dec unsettled at this
                        point in negot.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Paik proposed that formal agmt be signed 25 Feb. UNC proposes to make the
                        25 Feb agmt effective 26 Feb in order to convenience our funding and finance
                        people by avoiding a split day.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>New subj: Indications Paik will present draft of new law to assembly near
                        future for rationing of essentials. Apparently ROK Govt gaining
                        confidence.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Further info of significance will be forwarded as avail.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
